/*
	RMSTEST 12 — how does the engine round a fractional scaled value?

	The other half of preview-design Sec.15 item 7b. RMSTEST_11 settled the
	METHOD: scaling uses exact map area, measured at 829 for declared 400 on
	Small (400 × 20736/10000 = 829.44), against 840 for the guide's rounded
	ratio column. But 829.44 floors to 829 AND rounds to 829, so that run says
	nothing about which.

	Sec.4 currently pins "round half up, floor at 1 for any attribute whose
	declared value was >= 1". The round-half-up half is unverified.

	THE ARITHMETIC (run on SMALL, 144x144 = 20736)
	  500 × 20736/10000 = 1036.8
	    floor -> 1036
	    round -> 1037

	One object apart. Nothing but an exact count could read that, which is the
	whole reason tools/scenario-probe exists.

	READ IT WITH THE PROBE
	  python tools/scenario-probe/probe_scenario.py <saved scenario>
	  Read GOLD (66). Ignore id 1358 — GRASS terrain decoration, ~1196 of them,
	  unrelated.

	  1036 -> the engine truncates. Sec.4's "round half up" is wrong; change it
	          to floor, and check Sec.6.2/6.4's budgets for the same assumption.
	  1037 -> round half up. Sec.4 stands as written, fully verified.
	  840-ish or 1050 -> something is wrong with the run, not the rounding;
	          1050 would be 500 × 2.1, i.e. the ratio model, which RMSTEST_11
	          already refuted. Re-check the map size is Small.

	  A count one or two BELOW the expected value is worth a second seed before
	  concluding: 1037 objects on 20736 tiles is dense enough that an occasional
	  placement failure is more plausible here than in RMSTEST_11.

	Identical to RMSTEST_11 in every other respect, deliberately — one variable.

	RUN ON: Small, 2 players.
*/

<PLAYER_SETUP>
random_placement

<LAND_GENERATION>
base_terrain GRASS

create_player_lands
{
	terrain_type GRASS
	base_size 3
	number_of_tiles 1
	circle_radius 45 0
}

<OBJECTS_GENERATION>

create_object GOLD
{
	number_of_objects 500
	set_scaling_to_map_size
}
